# Plan: Prevent duplicate Fragment Title for cloned cards in M@S Studio

## Summary
When a card is cloned in M@S Studio, the clone dialog pre-fills the title field with the original title, which can result in two fragments sharing the same Fragment Title under the same tag path. This plan adds a uniqueness check scoped to the parent path: before the clone dialog opens, a unique title suggestion is computed by scanning existing fragments and incrementing a numeric suffix (`-1`, `-2`, …) until a free slot is found. The dialog pre-fills this suggestion; users may still edit it freely. The same deduplication is also applied inside `copyFragment()` in the repository as a safety net.

## Task Description
Introduce a `generateUniqueTitle(baseTitle, parentPath)` method on `MasRepository` that:
- Searches all fragments under `parentPath` using the existing AEM search API
- Collects their titles
- Parses the `baseTitle` to strip any trailing `-N` numeric suffix and determine the canonical base
- Increments a counter suffix (`-1`, `-2`, …) until a title is found that does not exist in the result set
- Returns the unique title string

Wire this into:
1. `showClone()` in `mas-fragment-editor.js` — pre-populate `this.titleClone` before opening the dialog, and update the dialog `value` binding to reflect `this.titleClone`
2. `showClone()` in `editor-panel.js` — same change for the parallel editor panel component
3. `copyFragment()` in `mas-repository.js` — if `updatedTitle` is empty/falsy, call `generateUniqueTitle` and always save with a unique title (safety net in case the dialog is bypassed)

## Relevant Files

| File | Action | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| `studio/src/mas-repository.js` | Edit | Add `generateUniqueTitle()` method; update `copyFragment()` to use it as a fallback |
| `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js` | Edit | Pre-populate `titleClone` in `showClone()`; update clone dialog `value` binding |
| `studio/src/editor-panel.js` | Edit | Same as above for the parallel editor panel |
| `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js` | Edit | Add unit tests for `generateUniqueTitle()` |

## Step by Step Tasks

### 1. Add `generateUniqueTitle` to `mas-repository.js`

Add the following method to `MasRepository`:

```js
/**
 * Finds a unique fragment title scoped to a parent path.
 * Strips any existing trailing -N suffix from baseTitle, then increments
 * until a title is not taken by any fragment in parentPath.
 * @param {string} baseTitle - The original fragment title
 * @param {string} parentPath - The parent folder path to scope uniqueness
 * @returns {Promise<string>} A title that does not conflict with existing fragments
 */
async generateUniqueTitle(baseTitle, parentPath) {
    // Strip existing trailing numeric suffix: "foo-2" -> "foo", "foo-bar-3" -> "foo-bar"
    const suffixMatch = baseTitle.match(/^(.*)-(\d+)$/);
    const canonical = suffixMatch ? suffixMatch[1] : baseTitle;

    // Collect titles of all fragments in the parent path
    const existingTitles = new Set();
    try {
        const generator = this.aem.sites.cf.fragments.search({ path: parentPath });
        for await (const items of generator) {
            for (const item of items ?? []) {
                if (item?.title) existingTitles.add(item.title);
            }
        }
    } catch {
        // If search fails, return a best-effort suffix-1 title
        return `${canonical}-1`;
    }

    // Return canonical if not taken, otherwise increment
    if (!existingTitles.has(canonical)) return canonical;
    let counter = 1;
    while (existingTitles.has(`${canonical}-${counter}`)) {
        counter++;
    }
    return `${canonical}-${counter}`;
}
```

Place this method alongside `copyFragment` in the same class.

### 2. Update `copyFragment` in `mas-repository.js` as a safety net

After obtaining `result` from `this.aem.sites.cf.fragments.copy(this.fragmentInEdit)`, always resolve a unique title before deciding to save:

- Compute `parentPath = this.fragmentInEdit.path.split('/').slice(0, -1).join('/')`
- If `updatedTitle` is falsy, resolve via `generateUniqueTitle(this.fragmentInEdit.title, parentPath)`
- If `updatedTitle` is provided, use it as-is (the user typed it in the dialog)
- Set `needsSave = resolvedTitle !== result.title || osi` (always save if the title differs from what AEM produced)
- Update `result.title = resolvedTitle` before saving

This ensures no duplicate title even if `confirmClone` is called programmatically without a `titleClone`.

### 3. Pre-populate `titleClone` in `showClone()` — `mas-fragment-editor.js`

In `showClone()` (around line 1088), before setting `showCloneDialog = true`:

```js
async showClone() {
    if (Store.editor.hasChanges) {
        const confirmed = await this.promptDiscardChanges();
        if (!confirmed) return;
    }
    const parentPath = this.fragment.path.split('/').slice(0, -1).join('/');
    this.titleClone = await this.repository.generateUniqueTitle(this.fragment.title, parentPath);
    this.showCloneDialog = true;
    Store.showCloneDialog.set(true);
}
```

### 4. Update clone dialog `value` binding — `mas-fragment-editor.js`

In `get cloneConfirmationDialog` (around line 1232), the textfield currently has:

```html
value="${this.fragment.title}"
```

Change it to:

```html
value="${this.titleClone}"
```

This ensures the dialog input reflects the pre-computed unique title.

### 5. Pre-populate `titleClone` in `showClone()` — `editor-panel.js`

Same change as Step 3 applied to `showClone()` in `editor-panel.js` (around line 620):

```js
async showClone() {
    if (Store.editor.hasChanges) {
        const confirmed = await this.promptDiscardChanges();
        if (!confirmed) return;
    }
    const parentPath = this.fragment.path.split('/').slice(0, -1).join('/');
    this.titleClone = await this.repository.generateUniqueTitle(this.fragment.title, parentPath);
    this.showCloneDialog = true;
    Store.showCloneDialog.set(true);
}
```

### 6. Update clone dialog `value` binding — `editor-panel.js`

In `get cloneConfirmationDialog` in `editor-panel.js` (around line 881), the textfield currently has:

```html
value="${this.fragment.title}"
```

Change it to:

```html
value="${this.titleClone}"
```

### 7. Add unit tests for `generateUniqueTitle` — `mas-repository.test.js`

Add a `describe('generateUniqueTitle', ...)` block that covers:

- Returns the canonical base title when it does not exist in the parent path
- Returns `canonical-1` when the canonical title already exists
- Returns `canonical-2` when both canonical and `canonical-1` already exist
- Strips an existing `-N` suffix from the input title before computing the base
- Returns `canonical-1` if the search API throws

Use the existing `createAemMock` and `createRepository` helpers; extend the AEM mock's `search` stub to return an async generator.

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Cloning a card whose Fragment Title already exists in the parent path opens the dialog pre-filled with `<original>-1` (or the next available suffix)
- [ ] Cloning `lucy-card-1` when `lucy-card-1` and `lucy-card` both exist produces `lucy-card-2` (canonical is `lucy-card`, next free is `lucy-card-2`)
- [ ] Cloning a card whose title does not collide opens the dialog pre-filled with the original title unchanged
- [ ] The original card's Fragment Title is not modified
- [ ] Manually editing the pre-filled title in the clone dialog works without restriction
- [ ] After clone, no two cards under the same path share the same Fragment Title
- [ ] `generateUniqueTitle` unit tests pass: no-collision, single-collision, multiple-collision, strip-suffix, search-error fallback

## Validation Commands

```
node --check studio/src/mas-repository.js
node --check studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js
node --check studio/src/editor-panel.js
node --check studio/test/mas-repository.test.js
```

